<title>POLAND: Polish bourse seen extending two-session gain.</title>
<headline>Polish bourse seen extending two-session gain.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish bourse was expected to extend its two-session gain, signalled by Monday's strong buying after price-fixing of large-cap stocks such as BRE, Bank Slaski and Elektrim.</p>
<p>Analysts said stocks posting good October earnings results late Monday could also see rises.</p>
<p>But they also said small but attractive offers on the primary market of construction firms  Energoaparatura SA and Elektromontaz Warszawa SA and road builder  GPRD SA could draw capital from stocks this week.</p>
<p>-- Steven Silber +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
